The Mojito FormatJS validation parser is a Java port of the parser state
machine from @formatjs/icu-messageformat-parser 3.5.10 and the validation-
relevant grammar from @formatjs/icu-skeleton-parser 2.1.9.

Upstream project: https://github.com/formatjs/formatjs
Upstream packages and versions:
- packages/icu-messageformat-parser 3.5.10
- packages/icu-skeleton-parser 2.1.9

The Java port changes the implementation language and adds a configurable
maximum nesting depth for bounded validation. It does not include the FormatJS
renderer or locale-formatting implementation. Locale-dependent `j` date/time
skeleton resolution is intentionally outside this locale-neutral validation
parser. The port is deterministic and does not reproduce upstream JavaScript
regular-expression state leakage after a failed skeleton parse.
